    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d557">

                <pb facs="1305" n="1191" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg1191"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/9–143:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Minister Resident at Allied Force
                        Headquarters</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Macmillan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the British Foreign Office
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d557-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-31">August 31,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have informed General Eisenhower.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>It is impossible to foretell the circumstances in which signature if any
                        is likely to take place and no arrangements can yet be made. I <pb
                            facs="1306" n="1192" xml:id="pg1192"/> therefore trust that the Greek
                        Government will not send an officer from the Middle East or anyone else for
                        the present.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>In case of need I will telegraph direct to Leeper as you suggest.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d557-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d557-f1-content">
